clustine-structures

Most of this crate is adapted from SteelMC
(https://github.com/Steel-Foundation/SteelMC), branch `26.3` at commit
`885c4b3e60ed79862c37311780774f76806cb714`. Steel: A high-performance Minecraft
server implementation written in Rust. Copyright (C) 2026 Alve Jeansson and
contributors. Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or
(at your option) any later version; see `LICENSE` at the root of this
repository. The files that were adapted say so at their head.

Adapted from SteelMC's steel-worldgen/src/structure/, each from the file of the same
name, with its imports changed, its tests left out (they rest on SteelMC's
registries) and what the pinned 26.3 jar does otherwise put right where the judge
found it: src/piece.rs, src/utils.rs, src/single_piece.rs, src/desert_pyramid.rs,
src/end_city.rs, src/fortress.rs, src/igloo.rs, src/jungle_temple.rs,
src/mineshaft.rs, src/nether_fossil.rs, src/ocean_monument.rs, src/ocean_ruin.rs,
src/ruined_portal.rs, src/shipwreck.rs, src/stronghold.rs, src/swamp_hut.rs and
src/mansion/. Their comments are SteelMC's.

src/geometry.rs is adapted from SteelMC's steel-utils (rotation.rs, direction.rs,
geometry.rs, types/), without the crate `glam` those are built on. src/compat.rs and
src/context.rs keep the names and shapes of SteelMC's registry of structures and of
its `StructureGenerationContext`, over Clustine's data and terrain, so that the
adapted files read as they did.

src/placement.rs, src/jigsaw.rs and src/lib.rs were written from the classes of the
pinned server jar, with SteelMC's placement.rs, jigsaw.rs, generator.rs and start.rs
read beside them; each says so at its head.

The data the crate computes with is Mojang's, from `clustine-worldgen-data`; see
NOTICE.md at the root of the repository. No block of a structure template is in
this repository (ADR-0019).
